        "thinking": "All remaining errors are in `packages/db/src/` — not in the CF package source files. These are pre-existing issues in the DB package when compiled under the bundler/ES module config (it uses NodeNext normally). These are not errors in the CF Worker code itself.\n\nThe CF package source files (`packages/deploy-cloudflare/src/**`) are now error-free. The errors in `packages/db/src/` are because we're now type-checking those files too (they get pulled in via imports), but they're pre-existing issues from different module resolution settings.\n\nThe proper solution is to add `skipLibCheck: true` (already in base) AND exclude the workspace packages from being directly type-checked. \n\nI'm realizing that `skipLibCheck` won't help here since the DB package files are being treated as source files rather than library files. I could exclude those workspace packages from the tsconfig, but that might break type resolution if we actually need those types. Let me think through what the right approach is here.\n\nThe real issue is that TypeScript Project References would be the proper solution for a monorepo setup, but that's a bigger refactor. For now, since Wrangler will handle the actual build and we're just using tsc for type-checking, I can accept the DB errors and focus on fixing only the errors in the deploy-cloudflare source itself.\n\nI'll add an exclude pattern to the tsconfig to skip type-checking the packages/db directory entirely.",
